virtual dom is a javascript representation of actual dom.when the state/props changes of a react component. the react creates a virtual dom and compare it with old virtual dom . it identifies what has changed and update require part of the dom. instead of update the entire part of the page

Suppose your page has:

Name: Renuka
Age: 25
City: Bangalore

If only the age changes:

Age: 25 → 26

React determines that the Age part changed and updates the necessary DOM rather than rebuilding the entire UI.

What is reconciliation?
Reconciliation is the process React uses to compare the previous Virtual DOM with the new Virtual DOM and determine what changes need to be applied to the actual DOM.

What is diffing in React?
Diffing is the process of comparing the previous Virtual DOM with the new Virtual DOM to identify the differences.

Diffing → find differences
Reconciliation → determine and apply required UI updates

Does React update the entire DOM?
No a state change can cause a rerender the component, but doesnot mean that react entire browser dom recreate, react determine and update necessary dom changes

Re-render ≠ entire DOM replacement

